  "description": {
    "text": "Pokémon TCG: Rumble, a boxed multiplayer game released on 2 December 2009 alongside the WiiWare video game Pokémon Rumble. Up to seven players set its 16 Pokémon out on a Battle Royale playmat, placed markers on the ones they thought would outlast the others, and rolled Energy and Target dice to decide each attack, scoring for each Knock Out and most for the last Pokémon standing. The box held the 16 cards, the playmat, four Energy dice, a Target die and 14 player markers.\n\nThe cards use the video game's pictures of the Pokémon and carry a foil Rumble logo; three of them are all-foil. Japan had the set first, in July 2009, as Melee! Pokémon Scramble × Pokémon Card Game.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "ICv2: Preview of 'Pokemon Trading Card Game: Rumble' (13 November 2009)",
        "url": "https://icv2.com/print/article/16268"
      },
      {
        "title": "PocketMonsters.net: Pokémon Rumble TCG (16 November 2009)",
        "url": "https://pocketmonsters.net/news/674"
      },
      {
        "title": "WikiDex: Pokémon Rumble (TCG)",
        "url": "https://www.wikidex.net/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Rumble_(TCG)"
      },
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: Pokemon Rumble Cards",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/pokemon-rumble-cards/10772"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "The Pokémon Rumble set symbol, and a number out of 16",
